The 1909–10 Scottish football season was [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]]'s 22nd season of competitive football, in which they competed in [[Scottish Division One]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.londonhearts.com/scores/a1910/celtic1910.htm|title=Results for Celtic for 1909-10|website=www.londonhearts.com}}</ref> They won the League for the sixth time in a row, which was a record at the time and would remain so until Celtic itself beat it by [[Nine in a row|winning nine league championships in a row from 1966 to 1974]].

After having reached the final of the [[Scottish Cup]] for the previous three seasons, Celtic fell short of it losing 3-1 to [[Clyde F.C.|Clyde]] in the semi-final.

Celtic won the [[Glasgow Cup]], defeating [[Rangers F.C.|Rangers]] 1-0 in the final.

